                <pb facs="0977" n="863" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg863"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stockton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-10T17:00:00+01:00">April 10, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 10—2:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>34. Referring to my telegram number 26, April 2, 1 p.m., Foreign Office has
                    formally advised me its readiness to exchange ratifications and has inquired
                    when Legation will be prepared to do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
